WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
<v Mike>Ikari 3, The Rescue.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.900
<v Mike>It is the end of the 20th century.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:29.360
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.500
<v Hosts>I'm Mike.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.480
<v Hosts>And I'm Sean.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.000
<v Mike>Sean, drop the Warriors.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:35.720
<v Mike>It's cleaner that way.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.800
<v Mike>Okay. What happened to our Ikari guys?

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.340
<v Sean>Um, well, there's still more than one though.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.280
<v Mike>Yeah, but like, they used to be the Ikari Warriors.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.640
<v Mike>Now it's just Ikari.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.340
<v Sean>You know what?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.760
<v Sean>I didn't even really clock that.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.680
<v Sean>I see now that it says Ikari 3, The Rescue.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:07.400
<v Sean>Um, but you're still, you know, you're still your shirtless, like, uh, non, non, uh, copyright material Rambo.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:14.960
<v Mike>It's just so funny that you say you're still your shirtless, non copyrightable Rambo, but like, yet they just came back from outer space.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.180
<v Mike>Remember the second game?

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.460
<v Sean>I very barely remember the second game.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.700
<v Mike>This is like, this is just, we've had some issues, right?

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.180
<v Mike>With sequels just completely changing the kind of game you get.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.260
<v Mike>And, uh, we've talked about that at length on this podcast.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.280
<v Mike>We're not going to get into it here.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.640
<v Mike>But this is a trilogy that wants nothing to do with each other.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:43.880
<v Mike>Like, the first Ikari Warriors was just like some good old fashioned top down run and gun stuff with some vehicles along the way.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.720
<v Mike>Then they went to space for Ikari Warriors 2.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.980
<v Sean>Remember being a bit more RPG like.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.020
<v Mike>They totally jumped the shark there.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.680
<v Mike>And now with Ikari 3, we're back on Earth.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.140
<v Mike>So it looks like, oh, okay, 2 was just a mistake.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.540
<v Mike>And, uh, we're going to correct the wrongs and go back to the, uh, the foundation that the original set.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.980
<v Mike>Except for, where the hell are their guns?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:13.900
<v Sean>Yeah, this kind of feels like, I mean, I'm off the top of my head, I'm having trouble coming up with an example right now.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:24.820
<v Sean>But when a, like an IP feels like, oh, we got to go back to our roots, but like even more rooted than the original game might have been.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.260
<v Sean>Like, do you have an example of something like this?

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.840
<v Mike>Of something going back to its roots?

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.860
<v Sean>But like, even, like even more rooted than its roots are.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.600
<v Mike>Right. Yeah, I guess that's like Breath of the Wild.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.000
<v Sean>Yeah. Okay, yeah.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.420
<v Sean>Like, let's do, it's like this.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.400
<v Sean>This is the Breath of the Wild of Ikari Warriors.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.500
<v Mike>There you go. Wow, they would love to have that on the back of their box for the, uh, for the anthology collection.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.420
<v Sean>No guns.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:59.120
<v Sean>And you know what? It also gets rid of the, the one complaint that I remember I had from when we originally recorded was that like, you always have to shoot in the direction you're walking.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.080
<v Sean>Um, so they just took the gun away.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.080
<v Mike>Yeah, they said that's not working anymore for Sean.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:13.640
<v Mike>What if we just made it so that you can't shoot a gun at all and you just go around punching and kicking and everybody looks like they're just doing Fred Astaire tap dancing.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.280
<v Mike>Uh, because everybody, you and the computers are all like, you know what this game's all about?

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.480
<v Sean>The jump kick.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:39.300
<v Sean>The spinning jump kick. It is so fucking funny watching jump kicks getting countered by jump kicks and you're just, it's sort of like, uh, watching like a, like a mosh pit of people that are like doing that hardcore dance where you just sort of punch at each other.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:47.340
<v Sean>And it's just complete chaos and people get hit and they, but they, they look, they get hit, but they also look goofy doing it.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.980
<v Sean>And that's what this game is like.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:57.900
<v Mike>Yeah. The only thing funnier is when you like have too many enemies and one starts punching you and then you just kind of get like stun locked into like being punched by everybody.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.100
<v Mike>And there's like, how the hell do I get out of this?

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.400
<v Mike>Like everybody's just ragging on me and it never happens the other way.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.860
<v Mike>You're not able to like successfully punch like seven people at the same time.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:21.380
<v Sean>You may not be able to do that, but you can like, like mess with the Z axis a little bit and sort of like just spam your jump kick, which kind of protects you from getting stun locked.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.280
<v Sean>That's true.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:28.380
<v Sean>And also allows you to sort of intersect big groups of guys.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.120
<v Sean>Um, but it's not, it's not a hundred percent.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:38.740
<v Mike>It doesn't always work. And what's funnier too, is like, you know, we always joke about these one man army things, right?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.940
<v Mike>Where, uh, it's just one guy who's just been told like, Hey, we, we can't send anybody else.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.280
<v Mike>It's just you. You're our last hope.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.200
<v Mike>Go save the world.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.120
<v Mike>And usually all they have is a gun, right?

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.460
<v Mike>This time you don't even have a gun.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:57.700
<v Mike>And the army is like, okay, so we have to make this a fair fight for them because they're all using their fists too.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:58.860
<v Mike>It's like, where are their guns?

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:06.300
<v Mike>What happened? Is this like, did we make a peace deal at the end of the car warriors too in space where the aliens like took away all of our guns?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.120
<v Sean>I just, sorry.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:25.800
<v Sean>I'm watching a play through while we talk and I just watched a whole squadron of otherwise normal looking soldiers just sort of do a choreographed dance of kicks towards you.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.460
<v Mike>Yeah. You put a little Moses supposes behind that and it looks like it's synced to the music.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.160
<v Mike>Okay. Um, yeah.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:38.660
<v Sean>Okay. So, I mean, you mentioned something about what, what could even be happening in this game.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.760
<v Sean>Do you know what's going on in the story?

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:47.140
<v Sean>Like I, Oh yeah, it has cut scenes, but I'd have no idea what's happening in them.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:56.440
<v Sean>I feel like there's some hieroglyphics going on in the beginning where it's given you like sort of a visual representation of the story, but I could not parse it.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:09.620
<v Mike>Well, as I mentioned, Sean, uh, as the back of the box for the game at the start of the episode, uh, it is the end of the 20th century and a worldwide economic recession has wreaked havoc with the nation and the planet.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:22.940
<v Mike>So this thing's trying to like predict the.com bubble a little early, uh, and the, all this, um, anarchy and, uh, recession has created a new organization called crime ghost.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.660
<v Mike>Well, now that's fucking cool.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.820
<v Sean>Right. Like anonymous.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.560
<v Mike>Yeah, I guess.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.520
<v Sean>Yeah. Right. It's like the V for vendetta guys.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.840
<v Mike>Like they're the crime ghost.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.860
<v Mike>Okay. And crime ghost leader Faust has now, uh, kidnapped the president's daughter.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:47.880
<v Mike>Uh, whose name is Elise and he has threatened to execute her unless the president resigns.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.920
<v Mike>So far I'm on the side of the crime ghost here.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:07:00.820
<v Mike>Like we, we, we have an economic recession and, uh, you know, all this stuff is going on and all he wants is the president to resign.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.100
<v Mike>I know we don't give in to terrorist demands.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.840
<v Mike>This seems like a light one.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.720
<v Mike>Like just give up.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:09.040
<v Mike>It's not saying like, and I'll take your place.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:16.140
<v Sean>Yeah. He just wants like the vice president to be president or something, I guess, if that's how we understand it.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.060
<v Sean>This sounds very Kojima.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.340
<v Mike>Yeah, it does. It really does.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.500
<v Mike>Because here's the funny thing too.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.900
<v Mike>It's not like if he resigns, they won't just have an election, right?

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.500
<v Mike>Like they're going to have another election.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.300
<v Mike>It's not like, they're not going to be like, Oh, well he resigned.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.880
<v Mike>So I guess, uh, Faust, like you're in charge now, right?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.060
<v Mike>It's not like how things work.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:44.140
<v Sean>He just, he's just calling for, uh, he's just calling for there to be a, a trial, like a, a, sort of an impeachment.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:50.260
<v Mike>So how much of the plot of Akari three, the rescue is lifted onto resident evil four?

00:07:52.100 --> 00:08:04.320
<v Sean>Well, I was, one of the reasons I mentioned metal gear solid was because, uh, there, there's like a fight with a cyborg ninja that just kept like sort of zipping, zapping around.

